{:schema_version 1
 :changes
 [{:id "ai-outcomes-and-run-costs"
   :date "2026-11-06"
   :component "app"
   :title "Keep real model answers, failures and measured costs"
   :summary "Keep actual child answers first, followed by compact outcome counts. Technical receipts stay in frozen details. Distinguish consumed output failures from uncertainty; continue independent authorized calls after known errors, but stop uncertainty without another parent request. Publish terminal answers, not intermediate plans. Captions separate measured parent/child reported, estimated and unpriced costs; direct streams receive only a terminal cost receipt. Retain safe statuses, caps, counters and timings without private payloads. No paid replay, silent budget increase or provider/default changes."
   :commands ["grok" "ai" "zen" "cf"]
   :requires ["Updated application; existing configured model/tool access"]
   :links ["https://github.com/yetibot/yetibot/pull/1327"
           "https://github.com/yetibot/yetibot/pull/1328"]}
  {:id "paid-text-model-selection"
   :date "2026-11-06"
   :component "app"
   :title "Choose paid Zen and text-capable Cloudflare models"
   :summary "Native Zen discovery defaults to paid text models with published input/output rates and supported API protocols. Select the exact model's Responses or Chat Completions protocol without following catalog URLs. Cloudflare native discovery exposes categories and filters text candidates before paging; stateless calls omit empty tool fields. Definite HTTP rejections no longer halt unrelated calls as unknown outcomes. Preserve no-retry safeguards, durable usage accounting and free-route revalidation. Successful Zen calls can estimate cost from returned tokens and known base rates; missing usage remains unavailable."
   :commands ["ai models zen" "cf models --categories"
              "cf models --category text-generation"]
   :requires ["Updated application; existing configured Zen/Cloudflare access"]
   :links ["https://github.com/yetibot/yetibot/pull/1326"]}
  {:id "ai-usage-ledger"
   :date "2026-11-06"
   :component "app"
   :title "Report AI usage by month or custom timeframe"
   :summary "Any trusted human can view bot-wide spend and usage by month or timeframe. Chat shows a compact summary and five model groups; Explore data keeps counters and caveats. Cover supported text, streaming, tool rounds, delegated models, classifiers, media, legacy calls and Gemini CLI sessions. Running bots require a durable pending row before inference; final ledger failures preserve completed results and leave honest uncertainty without paid retries. Keep reported USD, partial estimates and unpriced usage separate, with rollout warnings, native CLI scope and frozen reviewed data. No historical caption scraping, new billing credentials or provider-account invoice claims."
   :commands ["ai usage" "ai usage 2026-11"
              "ai usage 2026-11-01 2026-12-01"]
   :requires ["Upgraded core/application with the PostgreSQL usage ledger"
              "Trusted human chat actor"]
   :links []}
  {:id "ai-reply-routing-default-prices"
   :date "2026-11-05"
   :component "app"
   :title "Continue AI replies and compare default model prices"
   :summary "Plain human replies to fresh successful standalone AI/Grok/Zen answers inherit their resolved command, provider/model and safe options. Reply text stays literal; explicit commands switch branches. Recheck current policy, ownership and bounded context; ignore bots/errors/stale answers and duplicate turns. Paid routes make new paid requests; automatic free models must remain verified free, with no rotation or paid fallback. Any trusted chat user can explicitly select a global runtime default, including paid Zen models, with previous/new input/output list-rate comparisons; unknown prices say unavailable, and setting performs no inference. AI inspection and Zen model lists gain reviewed Explore data without credentials, endpoints, raw configs or private payloads."
   :commands ["zen Hello" "ai default zen gpt-5.4-mini" "ai default"
              "ai providers" "ai servers"]
   :requires ["Fresh retained Discord answer for implicit continuation"
              "Trusted direct chat for global defaults; normal model/tool policy"]
   :links []}
  {:id "weather-cron-alias-data"
   :date "2026-11-05"
   :component "app"
   :title "Follow reply conversations, inspect weather and manage schedules"
   :summary "Discord answers reply to their triggering command without pings. AI follow-ups read bounded same-channel reply ancestry, including visible V2 cards; unreadable chains fail before inference. Top-level zen gains conversation context but stays tool-free, while internal model calls remain stateless. Weather returns actual reviewed fields and explicit units for formatting suggestions. Cron supports current-channel list/get/create/update/delete with owner/admin writes, freshness and duplicate protection; no global controls or run-now. Scheduled commands cannot manage cron. Aliases/render preserve corresponding raw/reviewed data without publishing private fields."
   :commands ["zen What about Calgary?"
              "grok Run weather, inspect its data, and suggest a one-line alias."
              "grok List this channel's cron schedules."]
   :requires ["Trusted chat request and an enabled native toolset"]
   :links []}
  {:id "ai-tools-pagination"
   :date "2026-11-03"
   :component "app"
   :title "Browse tools and read complete formatted help"
   :summary "Tool lists show one-sentence overviews; inspect server/tool for complete formatted descriptions and parameter help. Long output has Previous/Next pages, balanced code fences and a complete Markdown download. Explore data retains only IDs and short summaries, plus flat parameter names/types/required flags for a selected tool, never raw catalogs or schemas. Collection operations keep corresponding raw/reviewed metadata with selected or reordered values; the viewer follows the completed pipeline, not intermediate catalogs. Navigation reads frozen reviewed text/data without discovery, tool calls or inference and preserves files, controls and the original elapsed caption. Metadata bounds, visibility and redaction remain."
   :commands ["ai tools" "ai tools alpaca" "ai tools alpaca/get_stock_snapshot"]
   :requires ["Discord rich replies and retained reviewed public text"]
   :links ["https://github.com/yetibot/core/pull/336"]}
  {:id "default-market-tools"
   :date "2026-11-03"
   :component "app"
   :title "Use approved market reads without selecting a toolset"
   :summary "Configured Alpaca read tools can join ordinary Discord search tools, so stock questions need no toolset flag. Server adapter rules filter connections and listings before discovery while preserving other toolset permissions. Explicit markets remains an Alpaca-only choice; trading/account tools stay disabled and tool availability never forces invocation."
   :commands ["ai What are the latest IEX trades for SPY and QQQ?"]
   :requires ["Configured approved Alpaca server included in the default toolset"]
   :links []}
  {:id "discord-inline-data-tree"
   :date "2026-11-03"
   :component "core"
   :title "Explore public data inside the original Discord answer"
   :summary "Explore data expands inline and becomes Hide data. The frozen public tree starts at two levels; Expand and Collapse change one level everywhere, with paging for large snapshots. Hiding restores the original card, files/media and elapsed caption. Data, tool and error panes replace one another without rerunning commands, refetching data or exposing private result maps. Controls expire with the command revision."
   :commands ["weather Seattle" "weather forecast Seattle" "version"
              "changelog --limit 2"]
   :requires ["Discord rich replies and a retained reviewed public snapshot"]
   :links ["https://github.com/yetibot/core/pull/334"]}
  {:id "discord-inline-tool-details"
   :date "2026-11-03"
   :component "core"
   :title "Toggle tool details inside your Discord answer"
   :summary "Show details expands the frozen public tool-call summary inside the original answer and becomes Hide details. Hiding restores the original card, files/media and elapsed caption. Inspection never reruns tools or reveals raw arguments/results; controls expire with the command revision. Long answers may be shortened only while details are open."
   :commands ["ai Explain this" "grok Explain this"]
   :requires ["Discord rich replies and retained sanitized AI progress"]
   :links ["https://github.com/yetibot/core/pull/333"]}
  {:id "grok-opt-in-threading"
   :date "2026-11-02"
   :component "app"
   :title "Grok replies here unless you choose a thread"
   :summary "Grok replies in the invoking channel or existing thread instead of creating one automatically. Use thread grok for all work in a thread, or grok ... | thread to move its final literal answer. Intermediate Grok answers flow as undecorated pipeline values without separate live publication. The --no-thread flag remains compatible, and caller context, model and tool policy stay unchanged."
   :commands ["grok Explain this" "grok Explain this | thread"
              "thread grok Explain this"]
   :requires ["Configured Grok provider or legacy xAI key"
              "Explicit thread delivery requires a Discord server text channel"]
   :links ["https://github.com/yetibot/yetibot/pull/1302"]}
  {:id "discord-result-viewers"
   :date "2026-11-02"
   :component "app"
   :title "Inspect safe results and pipe output into Discord threads"
   :summary "Native echo hi | thread sends the literal piped result into a confirmed message thread without executing it; later stages keep that destination and original caller permissions. Error details expands retained public failure stages/categories/HTTP status inside the original card; Hide restores it. No raw responses or private AI data are shown. Explore data provides bounded read-only weather/forecast and version/changelog snapshots with drill-down, Back and paging. Weather retains HTTP status for HTML errors and handles forecasts without a state code."
   :commands ["echo hi | thread" "echo hi | thread | echo result: %s"
              "weather Seattle" "version" "changelog --limit 2"]
   :requires ["Discord rich replies and core public-result support"
              "Thread pipes need a server text channel and thread permissions"]
   :links ["https://github.com/yetibot/core/pull/331"
           "https://github.com/yetibot/core/pull/332"]}
  {:id "discord-thread-timing"
   :date "2026-11-02"
   :component "core"
   :title "Run whole commands in Discord threads with shared elapsed timing"
   :summary "Use thread <command> to run a whole expression, including pipes, in a thread on your message. Edits and confirmed reruns reuse it. Original caller permissions and channel settings remain in force; uncertain thread creation never runs or retries the command. Rich command replies, errors, media, files and working cards share a measured elapsed footer without duplicate AI timing. Slack and intermediate pipeline values are unchanged."
   :commands ["thread echo hello | echo result: %s"
              "thread ai --provider zen Hello"]
   :requires ["Discord server text channel and thread permissions"]
   :links []}
  {:id "configured-zen-models"
   :date "2026-11-02"
   :component "app"
   :title "Zen honors the configured model and existing credits"
   :summary "An explicitly configured Zen model is no longer replaced by an automatic free model. GPT models use the Responses API without xAI-specific options; reported Zen costs appear in the existing tiny caption. Fresh free selection remains available only when no model is configured, with no silent paid fallback."
